<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  PROBE E3. Two unmeasured questions in one file, because they cannot be
  separated: (1) may a BKM body read a DECISION's variable at all, and (2) if a
  formalParameter is spelled the same as a decision, which wins?

  Question (1) has no obvious answer from the schema. Section 6.2's child list for
  a BKM is `variable? encapsulatedLogic? knowledgeRequirement* authorityRequirement*`
  with NO informationRequirement, so a BKM cannot DECLARE a dependency on a
  decision even if FEEL would let it read one. That makes "can it read one
  anyway" a genuinely open engine question, and a load-bearing one: if it can,
  the emitter has an undeclared edge it must either forbid or track.

      decision   base = 7
      bkm  reader(k)  = base + k       <<< question (1): reads a decision
      bkm  shadow(base) = base * 1000  <<< question (2): parameter spelled `base`
      decision   via_reader = reader(1)   -> 8 if a BKM may read `base`
      decision   via_shadow = shadow(2)   -> 2000 if the parameter shadows
                                          -> 7000 if the decision wins

  The two candidate answers for via_shadow differ by a factor of 3500, so
  whichever way it resolves is unmistakable, and neither is null.

  MEASURED 2026-07-31, and BOTH engines refuse question (1):
    KIE 8.44  : ERROR [ERR_COMPILING_FEEL] Error compiling FEEL expression
                'base + k' for name 'reader' on node 'reader': Unknown variable
                'base'. Validator AND build, i.e. compile time.
    Camunda 8 : parses, and via_reader evaluates to null.
  Question (2) resolves to the PARAMETER on Camunda (via_shadow = 2000, never
  7000 or 8000, in both cases).

  A CONSEQUENCE OF (1) WORTH KNOWING BEFORE READING THE KIE LEG: KIE's refusal is
  a whole-model compile error, so it never reaches question (2) in this file.
  Question (2) is therefore measured on KIE in collide-param-shadow-visible.dmn
  (probe E7), which asks it WITHOUT any BKM that reads a decision. The two files
  are a pair; E3 is the negative control for (1) and E7 is the positive for (2).

  Wired HarnessMustFail on BOTH legs.

  WHAT A FLIP MEANS. If (1) fails, nothing changes: the emitter never wanted an
  undeclared edge, and a refusal is the engine enforcing what checkDrg would
  anyway. If (1) SUCCEEDS, section 6.2's invariant list needs a new entry saying
  the emitter must not produce such a read, because the DRG will not show it. If
  (2) resolves to the decision on either engine, formalParameter names must be
  uniquified against decision names as well, which is the widening E1 rules out
  for inputData names only.
-->
<definitions xmlns="https://www.omg.org/spec/DMN/20191111/MODEL/" id="definitions_collide_param_decision" name="collide_param_decision" namespace="https://legalese.com/l4/dmn/collide_param_decision" exporter="hand">
  <inputData id="input_n" name="n">
    <variable id="input_n_var" name="n" typeRef="number"/>
  </inputData>
  <decision id="decision_base" name="base">
    <variable id="decision_base_var" name="base" typeRef="number"/>
    <informationRequirement id="ir_base_n">
      <requiredInput href="#input_n"/>
    </informationRequirement>
    <literalExpression id="decision_base_lit">
      <text>n + 7</text>
    </literalExpression>
  </decision>
  <businessKnowledgeModel id="bkm_reader" name="reader">
    <variable id="bkm_reader_var" name="reader" typeRef="number"/>
    <encapsulatedLogic id="bkm_reader_logic">
      <formalParameter id="bkm_reader_p1" name="k" typeRef="number"/>
      <literalExpression id="bkm_reader_lit">
        <text>base + k</text>
      </literalExpression>
    </encapsulatedLogic>
  </businessKnowledgeModel>
  <businessKnowledgeModel id="bkm_shadow" name="shadow">
    <variable id="bkm_shadow_var" name="shadow" typeRef="number"/>
    <encapsulatedLogic id="bkm_shadow_logic">
      <formalParameter id="bkm_shadow_p1" name="base" typeRef="number"/>
      <literalExpression id="bkm_shadow_lit">
        <text>base * 1000</text>
      </literalExpression>
    </encapsulatedLogic>
  </businessKnowledgeModel>
  <decision id="decision_via_reader" name="via_reader">
    <variable id="decision_via_reader_var" name="via_reader" typeRef="number"/>
    <informationRequirement id="ir_via_reader_base">
      <requiredDecision href="#decision_base"/>
    </informationRequirement>
    <knowledgeRequirement id="kr_via_reader">
      <requiredKnowledge href="#bkm_reader"/>
    </knowledgeRequirement>
    <literalExpression id="decision_via_reader_lit">
      <text>reader(1)</text>
    </literalExpression>
  </decision>
  <decision id="decision_via_shadow" name="via_shadow">
    <variable id="decision_via_shadow_var" name="via_shadow" typeRef="number"/>
    <informationRequirement id="ir_via_shadow_base">
      <requiredDecision href="#decision_base"/>
    </informationRequirement>
    <knowledgeRequirement id="kr_via_shadow">
      <requiredKnowledge href="#bkm_shadow"/>
    </knowledgeRequirement>
    <literalExpression id="decision_via_shadow_lit">
      <text>shadow(2)</text>
    </literalExpression>
  </decision>
</definitions>
